<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco del Rosario Sánchez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1817">1817</a>–<a href="/years/1861">1861</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francisco del Rosario Sánchez was a Dominican independence leader and member of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-trinitaria">La Trinitaria</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/secret-society">secret society</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-pablo-duarte">Juan Pablo Duarte</a>. On 27 February 1844 he proclaimed independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerta-del-conde">Puerta del Conde</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> and raised the new flag. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-santana">Pedro Santana</a> annexed the country to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1861, Sánchez led a rising against it and was captured and shot.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-del-rosario-sanchez.jpg" alt="Francisco del Rosario Sánchez" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: General de San Juan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Museo_de_Historia_y_Geograf%C3%ADa_-_Retrato_del_General_S%C3%A1nchez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Sánchez was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> on 9 March 1817. His mother, Olaya del Rosario Belén, was a free woman of colour; his father, Narciso Sánchez Ramona, a descendant of slaves, worked in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and meat trade. The parents married only in 1819, which is why he bore his mother's surname before his father's. He was taught first by his mother and then by the Peruvian priest Gaspar Hernández. Juan Pablo Duarte, a classmate, recruited him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-trinitaria">La Trinitaria</a>, founded in 1838.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Career</h2><p>When Duarte and others left the country on 2 August 1843 to escape Haitian persecution, Sánchez, who was ill, stayed behind in hiding and took over the leadership of the movement. On the night of 27 February 1844 his men took the Ozama Fortress, and at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerta-del-conde">Puerta del Conde</a>, after Matías Ramón Mella fired his blunderbuss, he raised the flag. He presided over the Central Government Board, and assured freed people who had mutinied under Santiago Basora that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> would not return.</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-santana">Pedro Santana</a> marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> and on 12 July 1844 drove the Trinitarios from the board. On 22 August Duarte, Sánchez and Mella were declared traitors and deported for life. He lived as a teacher in Curaçao until an amnesty granted by President Manuel Jimenes in 1848. Back home, he sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenaventura-baez">Buenaventura Báez</a> against Santana, was exiled again to Curaçao, returned in August 1856 and became governor of the province of Santo Domingo, and in 1859 was banished a third time, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-thomas-u-s-virgin-islands">Saint Thomas</a>.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>In 1861 Sánchez formed the Dominican Revolutionary Board and obtained from the Haitian president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fabre-geffrard">Fabre Geffrard</a> passage through Haitian territory and weapons for a force of 500 men. He entered through Hondo Valle on 1 June 1861. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> withdrew its support under threat from a Spanish squadron at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-au-prince">Port-au-Prince</a>, the expedition turned back. On 20 June Sánchez was ambushed near Hondo Valle by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> de Óleo, a former ally, wounded in the leg and groin, and captured.</p><p>A war council at San Juan under General Domingo Lazala tried the prisoners; Sánchez, conducting his own defence, asked that he alone be condemned. He was shot at San Juan de la Maguana on 4 July 1861 with some twenty companions, some of whom were finished off with machetes and clubs. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> withdrew from the country in 1865. Dominicans honour him with Duarte and Mella as a founder of the republic, and the Order of Merit of Duarte, Sánchez and Mella bears his name.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Francisco del Rosario Sánchez” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>On 27 February 1844 <b>Francisco del Rosario Sánchez</b> and Ramón Matías Mella proclaimed independence at the Puerta del Conde in Santo Domingo.</blockquote><a href="/state/first-dominican-republic">First Dominican Republic</a></li><li><blockquote>Early revolts were suppressed with executions, including that of <b>Francisco del Rosario Sánchez</b> in 1861.</blockquote><a href="/state/province-of-santo-domingo-1861-1865">Province of Santo Domingo (1861-1865)</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/dominican-republic">the Dominican Republic</a>. Died in San Juan de la Maguana, in what is now <a href="/countries/dominican-republic">the Dominican Republic</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=18.46,-69.94&amp;year=1845" aria-label="Santo Domingo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2655 1479 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Francisco del Rosario Sánchez"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3105 1749h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3105 1749h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=18.46,-69.94&amp;year=1845">What was here in 1845? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
